#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:134
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A turn is anything that arrives — a person's message, a tool result, a notification. The machine advances on turns rather than on a clock, because a session that has been told nothing has not changed."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:99
#. Diagram label
msgid "Actor established?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:65
#. Diagram label
msgid "Agent (playing the machine)"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:87
#. Diagram label
msgid "An actor picks up"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:166
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "An instance opened or closed, a bean claimed, a wait started or ended. All by REFERENCE: the bean and the instance are each the authority on themselves, and a status copied here would be free to contradict them. NO `cat-harness.processes:bean` on this step. It records that a claim happened; it does not claim."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:109
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ask who is acting"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:66
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Classifies every turn into exactly one of three effects at Gateway_TurnEffect — nothing changed, state changed, ending — a fresh judgement each time because a table cannot key on intent and a wrong read is corrected by the next turn. It records that a bean was claimed or an instance closed, at A_UpdateSession, but performs none of those actions itself: the record and the thing it describes are kept deliberately separate."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:177
#. Diagram label
msgid "Close the session"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:80
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Entered only when Gateway_ActorKnown cannot confirm an actor — the one fact in this whole record that the machine cannot recover by reading the repository — and answered once: the response is recorded so this lane is never re-entered for the same session, which is what keeps asking who is acting from becoming a repeated interruption."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:91
#. Diagram label
msgid "Establish who is acting"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:79
#. Diagram label
msgid "Human actor"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Is it established who is acting? `no` asks; `yes` opens the session record. A session is never opened for an actor it has not identified."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:193
#. Diagram label
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:199
#. Diagram label
msgid "nothing changed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:156
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Nothing changed, and saying so is the point. A record that stops being written looks exactly like an abandoned session; a refreshed timestamp with no other change says the session is alive and idle, which is a different fact and the commonest one."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:127
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Once the actor is known and the record is open, check that the coding agent acting here holds the permissions this instance's processes need, granted by a person and recorded, and ask for any that are missing. This is where initiating the harness for an actor secures them, rather than the first denied command. A run that finds them current returns without asking anything; the same process is called on demand when an action is denied later in the session. Vendor-neutral: the agent is a Tool, and its config is written through that Tool's adapter. Skill: agent-permissions."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:116
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the session record"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:178
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Records that the actor stopped. It does NOT resolve beans or complete instances: those outlive the session by design, and a machine that closed them on the way out would be asserting work finished because somebody went away."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:155
#. Diagram label
msgid "Refresh `updatedAt` only"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:126
#. Diagram label
msgid "Secure the agent's permissions"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:187
#. Diagram label
msgid "Session closed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:205
#. Diagram label
msgid "Session record"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:51
#. Diagram label
msgid "Session state machine"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:201
#. Diagram label
msgid "state changed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:133
#. Diagram label
msgid "Take in the turn"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:92
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The first step and not a formality: `actor` is the one field of the record that nothing else can supply. Every other field is recoverable by reading the repository; who is acting is not."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:145
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "THE non-deterministic point, and the reason this process exists. Three branches, and the agent chooses."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:110
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The one step that needs a person. Asked ONCE and recorded, never re-asked: `memory/interaction.json` and the record exist so that a preference stated once is not requested again, which is WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.7."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:203
#. Diagram label
msgid "the session is ending"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The shape of a session from the outside: establish who is acting, open a record for them, take each turn in, and write down only what actually changed. You are in this process for the whole of a session, underneath whatever else you are doing — it is the frame the other processes run inside. The first gateway is the one that matters: an agent that cannot say who is acting ASKS, because every later decision about permissions, preferences and language depends on an answer nobody guessed. The distinction between refreshing a timestamp and writing what changed is the diagram's whole content. A session record that logs every turn as a change cannot be read for what happened, and one that logs none cannot be read at all."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:144
#. Diagram label
msgid "What did the turn change?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:165
#. Diagram label
msgid "Write what changed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:117
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Writes `id`, `actor` and `startedAt`, with `open` and `claimed` empty. An empty `open` is the NORMAL state, not an unfinished one: an agent reading, answering or deciding is in no process at all."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn:195
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
